# single-source skills mirrors — derived state, regenerated from
# .ai-playbook/skills/ by materialise_skills.py on post-checkout / post-merge.
# All three are copies; none is a source. Committing one means every playbook
# bump lands as a diff of files nobody in this repo wrote, and any hand-edit
# here is silently overwritten on the next run — edits belong upstream in
# ai-playbook/skills/<name>/. Consumers onboarded before v0.17.0 may still
# track /skills/ from the RFC-0001 era, when it WAS the source; untrack it once
# with `git rm -r --cached skills/`.
/skills/
/.claude/skills/
/.gemini/skills/

# rendered MCP configs — LOCAL build artifacts (base+project+personal merge).
# Personal/tenant servers must never land in a committed file, so the rendered
# output is per-machine: regenerate with `python .ai-playbook/scripts/mcp/render.py`.
# The COMMITTED source of truth is mcp-servers.project.yaml (no personal) +
# ~/.config/mcp-servers.yaml (personal, local-only, never committed).
.mcp.json
.gemini/settings.json

# apply_config backup files (default location is next-to-original; the
# central layout under .ai-playbook-state/backups/ is covered above)
*.bak
*.bak.????-??-??T??-??-??Z
